भल् (or बल्) cl. 1. Ā. भलते, to describe or expound or hurt or give, Dhātup. xiv, 24 ;
 cl. 10. Ā. भालयते, to describe or behold;
to throw up (?), xxxiii, 27 (cf. नि-, निर्-, सम्-√ भल्).

बलाहक॑ or वलाहक॑, m. (Naigh. i, 10) a rain or thunder-cloud, any cloud, MBh.; Kāv. &c. (ifc. f. आ);
 one of the 7 clouds appearing at the destruction of the world, Cat.;
 Cyperus Rotundus, L.;
 a kind of crane (= बलाक), L.;
 a kind of snake, Suśr.;
 a kind of metre, Col.;
 N. of a serpent-demon, MBh.; Hariv.; Pur.;
 of a commander, Kād.;
 of one of the 4 horses of Viṣṇu, ib.;
 of a brother of Jayad-ratha, MBh.;
 of a Daitya, L.;
 of a mountain, Kathās.;

बाल्हिक or बाह्लिक, m. (pl.) N. of a people, MBh.;
 a king of the Bālhikas, ib.; Hariv.; Pur.;
 N. of a son of Pratīpa, Hariv.;
 (pl.) of a dynasty, BhP.;
 mfn. of the Balkh breed (as horses), MBh.; R.;
 n. (w.r. बाल्हक) saffron, L.;
 Asa Foetida, L.

बाल्हीक, बाह्लीक or वाह्लीक, m. (pl.) N. of a people, MBh.; R. &c.;
 a prince of the Bālhīkas, MBh.;
 N. of a son of Janam-ejaya, ib.;
 of a son of Pratīpa, ib.; Pur.;
 of the father of Rohiṇī (wife of Vasu-deva), Hariv.;
 of a Gandharva, L.;
 of a poet, Cat.;
 (ई), f. a princess or any woman of the Bālhikas (also N. of माद्री, q.v.), MBh.; Bālar.;
 mf(ई)n. belonging to or derived from the Bālhikas, L.;
 n. = बाल्हिक, L.

